From 3e914e4000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ant=C3=B3nio=20Sarmento?= <Keyaku@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: add the GPD XD+ device menu

The port needs a place to expose device-specific runtime switches, and the
ones it has are not settings any Android release has a home for: mini-HDMI
bring-up knobs for a path the vendor composer never drives on its own, and
the limits and wipe action for the Vulkan shader cache the graphics shim
keeps.

Everything here is property-only by design. The menu writes sys.xdplus.*
and persist.sys.xdplus.* and nothing else; the privileged work behind a
momentary action is done by an init service that watches those properties.
That is what lets the menu keep working with SELinux enforcing, where an
app-side file write or a direct service call would need policy of its own.

Three pages, each with its own fragment:

  * Display out         mini-HDMI resolution, vsync pacing, forced
                        validate, and the up/down actions. Labelled
                        experimental, because the built-in panel does not
                        render correctly while mirroring.
  * Vulkan shader cache per-app cache limit, a clear action, and the
                        shader-compile progress notification mode.
  * Top level           the group index, plus the receiver that turns
                        compile progress into a notification or a toast.

Squashed from the twelve commits on the xdplus-tweaks-menu branch: this is
one subject, and the intermediate states are not interesting to a fresh
checkout.
---
diff --git a/AndroidManifest.xml b/AndroidManifest.xml
